# Line endings are the repository's business, not each clone's.
#
# Everything stored here uses LF, because the machines that have committed to it
# had core.autocrlf=true. That is a per-clone setting: a contributor without it
# would commit CRLF and every line would show as changed. This makes the
# normalisation a property of the repository instead, so the stored form is LF
# regardless of who clones it, and Windows working copies still get CRLF.
* text=auto

# Marked rather than left to detection. text=auto classifies by looking for NUL
# bytes and would get these right, but SCEWIN_64.exe and its two drivers are the
# only path this project has to the firmware: a misclassification would rewrite
# bytes inside them, and the cost of being explicit is three lines.
*.ico binary
*.exe binary
*.sys binary

# Not binaries, but not text either. These are SCEWIN exports whose exact bytes
# are the point: the writer is required to reproduce them byte for byte outside
# the records it edits, so line-ending normalisation would break the tests that
# prove it.
tests/fixtures/*.txt binary
